    "title": "The Guardian view on Ordnance Survey maps: still a superior way to navigate the landscape | Editorial",
    "summary": "Ordnance Survey is marking 225 years since it first published a map, and an editorial celebrates its detailed paper maps as a distinctive way to read and navigate the British landscape. It sets the long craft of surveying against the fantasy of a map as large as the land itself.",
